35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data shows a clear bottleneck. Four out of eleven mornings required physical shoving.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The ledger confirms no capital funds exist. Any new infrastructure requires a direct levy on residents.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The minutes confirm the same flats held the covered spots for five years. No review was ever recorded.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The complaint log shows nine unresolved disputes. The neighbouring block’s secretary says their fee system caused two households to stop attending meetings.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,The frame trial showed the upper rail is hard to use. The rain data confirms only the eaves row is truly dry.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, the static allocation is the root cause. We need dynamic access.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, dynamic access requires management. The treasurer’s file shows that takes three hours a month.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"I agree. The lack of review is the problem. We need a transparent, rotating system.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, if the frame is hard to use, the upper spots are effectively unusable. We should only count the lower row.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, exactly. The upper rail is a trap. We should focus on the dry, lower spots and rotate them fairly.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The sticker register shows households are willing to pay for priority. We should monetize the convenience.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, monetization increases administrative burden. The ledger shows we have no buffer for that.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,I object to monetization. It favors the wealthy. A simple rotation of the dry spots is fairer.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, rotation is good, but we need a clear rule to prevent the ""time your exits"" behavior I warned about.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I support rotation. It’s simple, fair, and doesn’t require complex paperwork. Let’s just rotate the dry spots monthly.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
