60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is the only one that addresses the willingness to pay I found in the register.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A creates a new administrative burden. The ledger shows we cannot absorb that cost.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Option C is the most fair. It removes the static bias I found in the minutes.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is the most dangerous. It turns the lobby into a daily negotiation. I want to avoid that.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option C is simple. It doesn’t require constant monitoring. I can handle the annual draw without it becoming a monthly job.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the administrative burden is minimal. It’s just a payment record.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, ""minimal"" is relative. The treasurer’s file shows even small tasks take hours. I am not willing to risk the account’s stability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Asuka, I agree with Ryuji. We should not introduce a new financial layer. Option C is cleaner.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, Option C is better than B, but it still creates a ""winner"" and ""loser"" dynamic. Is that what we want?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, it’s better than the current chaos. And it’s a one-time task, not a monthly grind. I can manage it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for A. It’s the most efficient use of the resource.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I will vote for C. It is the least risky for the building’s finances.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I will vote for C. It addresses the fairness issue directly.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I will vote for C. It’s the least likely to cause the social friction I’m worried about.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I will vote for C. It’s simple, fair, and doesn’t require me to be the ""manager"" every month.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
